# CityVision — direct dependencies (source of truth).
# Python 3.10+.
#
# This is the *input* to pip-tools. The fully pinned lock is requirements.txt,
# generated with:   pip-compile requirements.in
# (in CI this is done on Linux via .github/workflows/lock.yml so the lock has
#  the correct platform-specific transitive deps.)
#
# ── PyTorch is installed SEPARATELY (not locked here) ───────────────────────
# It is platform/accelerator specific and would otherwise drag ~2.5 GB of CUDA
# packages into the lock. Install it explicitly:
#   CPU:  pip install torch==2.12.0 torchvision==0.27.0 --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu
#   CUDA: pip install torch==2.12.0 torchvision==0.27.0 --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu126

